-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled third-party component
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

jar/virtualPCR.jar is the in silico PCR engine, from the virtualPCR project
by Ruslan Kalendar: https://github.com/rkalendar/virtualPCR
It is distributed here unmodified, under the GNU General Public License
version 3. It is the build published on 2026-08-27, upstream commit
7208b64a376938d5e2b27edddebd2583fdd9fe80, file dist/virtualPCR.jar:

    SHA-256 96e9b06bcf7cc6b4aa0bb3d3fc2db983a22ec0d81edbc89035b4c6801b1c7a56
    https://github.com/rkalendar/virtualPCR/tree/7208b64a376938d5e2b27edddebd2583fdd9fe80

    Kalendar R., Shevtsov A., Otarbay Z., Ismailova A. (2024)
    In silico PCR analysis: a comprehensive bioinformatics tool for
    enhancing nucleic acid amplification assays.
    Frontiers in Bioinformatics 4:1464197. doi:10.3389/fbinf.2024.1464197

The source the author publishes for that build (src/ at the commit above) is
attached to each release of this app as virtualPCR-src-2026-08-27.zip. It
covers the program's front end; the search engine's classes (InSilicoPCR,
Melting, oligoparam, primer, LongIntHashMap) are not in it. Their source is
available from the author, and the GPLv3 entitles you to it.

The app's built-in engine (vpcr/core/thermo_engine.py) is an independent
search written for this project; it shares no code with the JAR.
